{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"metaphoric-late-creature","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\nOn an S3 ticket store (git-remote-s3 0.4.2, git 2.56.0), every reconciler pass whose lock remote is the S3 store fails at ref-lock acquisition. `_push_cas` (src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:733) pushes `<blob-oid>:<ref>` with --force-with-lease; git-remote-s3 passes the source side to `git bundle create`, which refuses a bare object id (\"Refusing to create empty bundle\", exit 128). Rebar sees only \"fatal: unknown error\" because the helper swallows git's message. The same push to a plain bare remote succeeds. Reproduced against moto and a real scratch bucket (since deleted); evidence: .rebar/worktrees/inv-s3-reflock/.rebar/scratch/inv-76869/.\n\nIntent: commit a06d00a / ADR 0031 (ticket 524d-00fa-66ef-4432) designed the lock as a bare-ref CAS proven only on GitHub and a local remote. ADR 0093 and docs/s3-backend.md later state reconcile \"works identically\" on S3 without a test.\n\nOn real S3 through the helper: a temporary named ref gives single-winner create; blob-to-blob renew/steal is always rejected (fast-forward only unless `+`, and `+` drops the lease); a commit chain whose parent is the observed lock gives single-winner renew/steal; delete has no lock or compare, so a release racing a steal both succeeded in 2 of 10 rounds.\n\nRelated, found in the same investigation:\n- The PUSH_PENDING hint says \"check connectivity to origin\" when the remote is not origin.\n- Two checkouts sharing one tracker can name different sync remotes (ADP: main checkout defaults to origin/GitHub, PR worktree uses s3tickets) with no warning.\n\n## Plan\nPending the maintainer's decision on the S3 lock design; written once it is made.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py\n- docs/adr/0093-s3-ticket-store-backend.md\n- docs/s3-backend.md","id":"7eaa-502b-3d0f-4b08","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler ref-lock fails on S3 ticket stores"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793330546360014001,"uuid":"f4288760-952e-43c1-8563-140094174466"}